# Wave W17-T (Route 132): stream rock — channel-edge rock standing in the lane\u2019s water: a neutral grey shore rock at the first current\u2019s channel edge, its joints plain and even — the current runs past it, not through it; foam collar at its base, the sea baked in around it. Route 132\u2019s own rock — the plainest of the three current rocks by design: split from Route 133\u2019s rapid rock by the joints (even vs long-drawn) and from Route 131\u2019s ancient tower-isle rock by register (worked channel stone vs weathered isle stone).
